n the request path). | RHAISTRAT-9013-E001 (KServe portion), RHAISTRAT-9013-E002 (Platform Operator portion) |\n| HLR-2 | P0 | A compliance evidence package (module inventory, build attestations, test results) is assembled and submitted through the security review board to the external certification lab. | RHAISTRAT-9013-E005 |\n| HLR-3 | P1 | CI enforces FIPS regressions: a gating check fails any serving-stack build that reintroduces non-validated crypto usage. | RHAISTRAT-9013-E003 (KServe builds), RHAISTRAT-9013-E004 (Platform Operator builds) |\n| HLR-4 | P2 | Documentation states the FIPS support posture and cluster prerequisites. | RHAISTRAT-9013-E006 |\n\nAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements. HLR-1 and HLR-3 each map to\ntwo epics because the work spans two components owned by different teams (epic\nboundary rule 1); each portion is independently schedulable in its own repo.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n- **Missing strategy sections.** The strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no\n  Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, no Non-Functional\n  Requirements, and no Technical Approach; the Affected Components section is a\n  bare list without per-component change/owner detail. The decomposition proceeds\n  from the HLRs and problem statement; epic acceptance criteria were derived from\n  the HLR text.\n- **Team assumption (verify before scheduling).** The Platform Operator epics\n  (RHAISTRAT-9013-E002, RHAISTRAT-9013-E004) are assigned to \"RHOAI Platform\" by\n  assumption — the strategy names no owning team for Platform Operator.\n- **Scope wording — \"serving data plane\".** The problem statement says \"KServe\n  components and the serving data plane link non-validated crypto libraries\", but\n  the Affected Components section lists only KServe and Platform Operator. The\n  serving data plane is treated as within the KServe component scope. If Serving\n  Runtimes images (vLLM, OpenVINO, Caikit — KServe dependencies per the\n  a