sfully through the existing serving-stack build\n  pipeline.\n- Functional verification on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster passes for the\n  inference request path, and the test results are recorded.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)** — All serving-stack images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters\n  using validated crypto modules (no non-validated crypto in the request path).\n  This epic delivers the KServe-component portion, including the serving data\n  plane within the KServe component scope.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":50259,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-879b2d36a972f8a6","agent_id":"a832036afe753050e","session_id":"507c58fb-94b1-4432-a69d-7f745e4ce707","uuid":"2d5d27f7-2f79-435f-b706-465800245010","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:09:02.294Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9013"}
