either can be compressed by\n  engineering effort. These are schedule risks on this epic, not acceptance\n  conditions — the acceptance criteria above are written at the\n  engineering-controlled endpoint (assembly and confirmed submission).\n- Security review board sign-off at the defined milestones is a mandatory human\n  process gate embedded in the submission route.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-2 (P0)** — A compliance evidence package (module inventory, build\n  attestations, test results) is assembled and submitted through the security\n  review board to the external certification lab. This epic delivers it in full.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":50259,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-879b2d36a972f8a6","agent_id":"a832036afe753050e","session_id":"507c58fb-94b1-4432-a69d-7f745e4ce707","uuid":"f4784b99-5478-4e6d-8d8d-9ee9bc63c008","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:09:22.933Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9013"}
