{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d7610018296e801","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E001\n3\ttitle: FIPS 140-3 remediation of KServe serving-stack images\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: KServe\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 0\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 3\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# FIPS 140-3 remediation of KServe serving-stack images\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic makes every KServe-component serving image run correctly on FIPS-enabled\n34\tOpenShift clusters using validated cryptographic modules, with no non-validated\n35\tcrypto in the request path. It covers auditing the KServe component images and the\n36\tserving data plane within the KServe component scope for non-validated\n37\tcryptographic library usage, remediating those usages against validated modules,\n38\tand verifying the remediated images on a FIPS-enabled cluster.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Audit all serving-stack images owned by the KServe component and produce a\n43\t  module inventory listing the cryptographic modules linked into each image and\n44\t  flagging every non-validated crypto usage in the request path.\n45\t- Replace or rebuild each non-validated crypto usage in the request path against\n46\t  FIPS-validated cryptographic modules.\n47\t- Rebuild the affected images through the existing build pipeline.\n48\t- Run functional verification of the inference request path (InferenceService\n49\t  deployment and serving) on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster and record the test\n50\t  results.\n51\t- Hand off the module inventory and the verification test results as inputs to the\n52\t  compliance evidence package.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- A module inventory exists covering every KServe-component serving image in the\n57\t  stack, listing linked cryptographic modules and flagging each non-validated\n58\t  usage in the request path.\n59\t- An image scan of every remediated image shows no non-validated cryptographic\n60\t  module linked in the request path.\n61\t- Remediated images build successfully through the existing serving-stack build\n62\t  pipeline.\n63\t- Functional verification on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster passes for the\n64\t  inference request path, and the test results are recorded.\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability\n67\t\n68\t- **HLR-1 (P0)** — All serving-stack images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters\n69\t  using validated crypto modules (no non-validated crypto in the request path).\n70\t  This epic delivers the KServe-component portion, including the serving data\n71\t  plane within the KServe component scope.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa6422f5086bb052","agent_id":"a090fa2fed4ccaea4","session_id":"507c58fb-94b1-4432-a69d-7f745e4ce707","uuid":"3de96e33-ebe6-4111-b9b4-bc5bb59fb757","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:11:33.894Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d7610018296e801","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
