fected images or request-path call sites\nthan a single sprint absorbs\") — a managed trade-off, within guideline.\n\n### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\nNo Investigation epics — correct per the Step 3 decision rule: the strategy's\nOpen Questions section is \"None on scope\", and the image-level crypto audit is\ninformational discovery whose outcome changes remediation volume, not which\nepics exist or what they do (rule 4: reclassified as scope/ACs on the\nremediation epics, with the module inventory as a deliverable feeding E005).\nEvery Implementation epic produces a concrete artifact (remediated images,\ngating check, evidence package, published docs). No `gated_by` anywhere and no\nbranch files, so gating metadata is trivially consistent. E006's\n`implementation_type: docs-authoring` is correct. The externally controlled lab\nand review-board cadence are correctly modeled as risks on E005, not as gates\non engineering work.\n\n### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\nAll six epics are Implementation type and carry `ai_signals` (9-signal rubric);\nno epic mixes signal sets. Frontmatter values match the ai-signals rationale\nfiles exactly for all six epics. Spot-checks against the rubric: E005's\n`existing_foundation: -1` (greenfield package — \"we have no compliance evidence\npackage\") and `external_dependency`/`human_process_gates: -1` (external lab,\nreview board) are well grounded in the strategy; E001/E003's\n`architecture_claims: +1` correctly cite\n`.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/kserve.md` (GA maturity,\n\"Konflux onboarded: yes\" — both verified present in the file); E002/E004/E006's\n`architecture_claims: 0` is the correct score because no context file covers\nPlatform Operator or Documentation (score 0 is valid only when no context file\ncovers the components — satisfied), and the coverage gap is disclosed in the\nsummary's Health Warnings rather than papered over with an invalid \"no claims\"\nrationale. `open_questions` values are