{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a971e978957ee895","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E003\n3\ttitle: FIPS regression gating check for KServe serving-stack builds\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: KServe\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 0\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# FIPS regression gating check for KServe serving-stack builds\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic adds a gating CI check to the KServe serving-stack build pipeline that\n34\tfails any build whose image reintroduces non-validated crypto usage in the request\n35\tpath, so FIPS regressions are caught before shipping rather than rediscovered at\n36\tthe next audit.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Implement a detection check that scans built serving-stack images for\n41\t  non-validated cryptographic module usage in the request path, using the same\n42\t  validated-module criteria as the remediation audit.\n43\t- Wire the check into the KServe serving-stack build pipeline as a gating step\n44\t  (a failed check blocks the build from shipping; it is not advisory).\n45\t- Validate the check with both test polarities: a deliberately non-compliant\n46\t  build fails, and a compliant build passes. The compliant test image may be\n47\t  constructed locally for the test (for example, rebuilt against validated\n48\t  crypto modules) — it does not need to come from the FIPS remediation work,\n49\t  so this validation does not sequence this epic on that remediation.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- The gating check runs on every KServe serving-stack build in the pipeline.\n54\t- A build whose image reintroduces non-validated crypto usage in the request path\n55\t  fails the check, demonstrated with a deliberately non-compliant test build.\n56\t- The check is gating: a failed check blocks the build from shipping.\n57\t- A build whose image contains only validated crypto in the request path passes\n58\t  the check.\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability\n61\t\n62\t- **HLR-3 (P1)** — CI enforces FIPS regressions: a gating check fails any\n63\t  serving-stack build that reintroduces non-validated crypto usage. This epic\n64\t  delivers the KServe-builds portion.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88842308451119e6","agent_id":"a004b5bbe6b2f479a","session_id":"507c58fb-94b1-4432-a69d-7f745e4ce707","uuid":"f1dfc5d2-78f4-4018-9dec-8684a3f47c60","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:17:01.546Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a971e978957ee895","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
