ot an approval step\".\n122\t- E006 `external_dependency: 0` with \"No upstream contribution or vendor\n123\t  coordination required\".\n124\t\n125\tIn each case the +1 condition holds, so the value should be +1, not 0. (E006's\n126\t`human_process_gates: 0` is the one defensible 0 — its mandatory technical\n127\treview is a human approval step, making neutral arguable.) This is not a \"1-2\n128\targuable values\" case: the rationales state the favorable condition verbatim\n129\twhile the values record neutral, which both breaks rationale-value consistency\n130\tand depresses the pipeline-computed implementability scores (e.g. E001's\n131\tcomputed score of 3 would be 5). E005 shows the decomposer uses the correct\n132\tpolarity on the unfavorable end (-1 for lab coordination and review-board\n133\tsign-off), so the favorable end being flattened to 0 is a rubric violation, not\n134\ta convention. Correction: re-score these eight signals to +1.\n135\t\n136\tMinor: E006 `architecture_claims: 0` is justified by \"no context file covers the\n137\tDocumentation component\", but the epic's scope documents the KServe serving\n138\tstack, which `.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/kserve.md`\n139\tcovers — per the rubric, 0 is only for epics no touched component has a context\n140\tfile for. Re-score against the architecture-context file and cite it in the\n141\trationale.\n142\t\n143\tOtherwise consistent: the type-appropriate `ai_signals` field is present on all\n144\tsix Implementation epics, ai-signals rationale files exist for all six, E002/E004\n145\t`architecture_claims: 0` is correct (no context file for Platform Operator),\n146\tE001/E003/E005 `architecture_claims: +1` cite kserve.md, and E005's unfavorable\n147\tsignals are correctly polarized. Computed `ai_implementability` /\n148\t`ai_implementability_score` values were not checked (pipeline-computed).\n149\t\n150\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n151\tEvery epic has testable ACs derived from the HLR text. Rule-mandated ACs:\n152\tRule 24 satisfied (E006: \"technically reviewed against the implemented FIPS\n153\tposture and passes that review\"); Rule 25 not applicable (no konflux-onboarding\n154\tchain), though E001/E002 carry build-pipeline-green ACs anyway; Rule 23 not\n155\tapplicable (crypto remediation, not capability replacement). The\n156\texternally-controlled schedule constraints (six-to-nine-month lab turnaround,\n157\treview-board cadence) are correctly recorded as E005 Risks/Notes and summary\n158\tHealth Warnings rather than acceptance criteria — E005's ACs are written at the\n159\tengineering-controlled endpoint (assembly and confirmed submission), exactly the\n160\tsoft-AC rule's required shape. The CI epics' ACs include both test polarities.\n161\tNo epic body references sibling epics by draft ID.\n162\t\n163\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n164\tAll strategy scope is covered: image remediation on FIPS-enabled clusters\n165\t(E001/E002), evidence package assembled and submitted through the security\n166\treview board to the external lab (E005, matching HLR-2's named route), CI\n167\tregression enforcement (E003/E004), and documentation of posture plus cluster\n168\tprerequisites (E006). Out-of-scope boundaries (workbenches/pipelines/training,\n169\tCommon Criteria) are respected and re-stated in E006's content outline.\n170\tStrategy-level context is carried forward, not dropped: external schedule risk →\n171\tE005 risks and Health Warnings; missing strategy sections and the team\n172\tassumption for Platform Operator → Health Warnings; the serving-data-plane /\n173\tServing Runtimes ambiguity → Health Warnings with an explicit revisit\n174\tcondition. Upstream multi-item outputs (module inventory, verification test\n175\tresults, signed attestations) are all consumed by E005's scope and ACs — no\n176\tsilently dropped items. The strategy has no Prerequisites & Process Gates\n177\tsection, and the HLR-4 documentation epic exists regardless. No conditional\n178\tbranches to check.\n179\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5bcae6cbb3811e1","agent_id":"ac682dbff8fca8d97","session_id":"507c58fb-94b1-4432-a69d-7f745e4ce707","uuid":"fc4421fa-cada-4677-b55b-eda5a3c04385","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:22:09.047Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2ef6e9bc64cef86","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Second revise RHAISTRAT-9013"}
